% The Magic rewrite of path(a, X)? keeps a seed, the magic rule passing the
% binding along edge, and the two adorned rules of path.  A limit of three
% generated rules is exceeded by the fourth.  A rule is charged to the
% predicate it was generated for, so the diagnostic names path/2.  A
% duplicate rule would be dropped before it was counted.

edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- edge(X, Y), path(Y, Z).

path(a, X)?
